<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 10px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Nutrition</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Why Is Nutrition Important?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Mediate school announcements for new students. Communication: Facilitate a discussion on a group project.<br>
            <b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can mediate school announcements on healthy practices for peers by using simple words and two languages if needed (e.g., explains "balanced" in both English and familiar language).
            Can facilitate a discussion on healthy eating by guiding turn-taking and encouraging classmates to share (e.g., encourages each student to share a favorite healthy food).
            Can help peers understand balanced diets by using simple words and two languages if needed (e.g., explains "balanced" using examples like eating both meat and vegetables during lunch or adding fruit for dessert.").
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of different Panamanian and international healthy foods (e.g., sancocho, arroz con pollo, a fruit salad, a balanced plate). Students quickly brainstorm (in pairs) one healthy food they would recommend to a new student and why. They practice offering dietary advice using "You should eat more fruits and vegetables for a balanced diet."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to explain a simple nutrition concept to someone who might not understand. For example, the teacher points to a picture of a fruit salad and says, "This is a fruit salad. It has many 'vitamins' and 'minerals.' If you eat fruits, you will have more energy. 'Vitamins' are like tiny helpers for your body." The teacher then models how to briefly clarify the meaning of "balanced" in simple English and perhaps with a quick example in a familiar language if a student asks for help, demonstrating how to mediate information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a new student asks, 'What are 'nutrients'?', how could you explain it simply?" (Possible answer: They are good things in food that help your body.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Should you only eat one type of food every day for a 'balanced diet'?" (No, because a balanced diet means eating a mix of foods like fruits, vegetables, and protein.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Nutrition".</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher presents a short, fictional school announcement about "Healthy Eating Habits at School." The announcement will contain advice using "should" and brief explanations using adverbial clauses and first conditional, possibly with some slightly more complex vocabulary for A2.4 (e.g., "metabolism," "antioxidants").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A projected "School Announcement" on healthy eating in a paragraph format, covering cafeteria choices and hydration, for example:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Genre: School Announcement / Notice</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Register: Semi-formal, informative</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Format: Short paragraph with bullet points for key advice.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will interpret and rephrase official school announcements about healthy practices for new students, ensuring clarity and understanding.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main message of this announcement?" "Who is this announcement for?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read statements about the announcement and mark them True or False (e.g., "The school recommends only eating processed foods for lunch.").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Modal "should" for giving advice, First conditional for facts, Adverbial clauses for justification.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> nutrition, health, benefits, balanced diet, fruits, vegetables, grains, vitamins, minerals, nutrients, protein, carbohydrates, hydration, improve, consume, advise, recommend, healthy, balanced, nutritious.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Practice stress in words like "metabolism," "antioxidant," "carbohydrate," "vitamin," and minimal pairs for /ɪ/ vs /iː/ (e.g., "bit/beat," "live/leave").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Offering dietary advice: "You should eat more fruits and vegetables for a balanced diet." Explaining nutrition benefits: "If we eat a mix of foods, it will give us energy and help us stay healthy."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled practice: Announcement Rewriting.</b> In pairs, students receive the school announcement from Stage 2. Their task is to rewrite key sentences from the announcement in simpler English, specifically for a "new student who is not fluent in English." They must use "should" for advice, first conditional, and adverbial clauses for justification. (e.g., "Students should consume a balanced diet because it improves concentration." becomes "You should eat different healthy foods because it helps you focus in class.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled practice: Explaining Key Terms.</b> The teacher provides a list of key vocabulary words from the announcement (e.g., "nutrients," "metabolism," "antioxidants," "fiber," "hydration"). In pairs, students practice explaining these words to each other using simple definitions and examples, like mediating for a peer. One student asks, the other explains, then they switch roles. They are encouraged to use a familiar language example if struggling, e.g., explaining "hydration" as "drinking enough water; como mantenerse hidratado." Focus on stress in multisyllabic words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair interaction/Peer check: Advice Exchange.</b> Students work in new pairs. Student A gives a piece of advice about healthy eating (e.g., "You should avoid processed foods because they are not good for your health."). Student B then rephrases this advice in an even simpler way, imagining they are explaining it to a younger sibling or a new, very shy classmate, using "If you eat well, you stay healthy" or similar simple structures. They check each other's clarity and use of target grammar.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task: Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial Project - Mediation Practice.</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in their "Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial" groups. Their task is to practice two specific mediation skills related to their project:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Facilitating Discussion:</b> One student in each group acts as a facilitator, guiding turn-taking and encouraging each member to share their ideas for the video tutorial's introduction, main steps, or a specific ingredient's benefits. The facilitator practices phrases like "What do you think, [name]?", "Can you explain that a bit more?", "Let's hear everyone's ideas first."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Mediating Project Information:</b> Groups choose one healthy ingredient from their recipe (e.g., oats, plantains, beans). Each group member takes turns explaining the nutritional benefits of that ingredient in simple words, using "should" for advice, first conditional, and adverbial clauses. They must simplify complex terms for a general audience, imagining they are explaining it in their video tutorial. For example, "Oats are a great source of 'fiber' because if you eat them, they will help your 'digestion'." They might also touch upon how this ingredient is used in Panamanian vs. other cultures to make it healthier (sociolinguistic competence).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Group collaboration and mini-presentation/role-play within the group, observed by the teacher.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme:</b> Directly applies the theme "Why Is Nutrition Important?" to their ongoing "Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial" project, integrating practical communication and mediation skills.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in giving advice and explaining, collaborative interaction in facilitating discussion, and effective mediation of nutritional information for their target audience.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on mediation skills, plus peer assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents a 1-minute "mediation segment" from their "Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial." This segment should include:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student facilitating a brief discussion (e.g., about adding an ingredient).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Another student explaining a key healthy ingredient or step in simple English, offering advice using "should" and explaining benefits with "if... will" or "because." They must demonstrate mediating complex info.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear stress on multisyllabic words and distinction of minimal pairs (e.g., "vitamin," "protein," "bit/beat").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> (nutrition, healthy, balanced diet, fruits, vegetables, benefits, protein, carbohydrates, hydration).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target grammar:</b> "should" for advice, first conditional, adverbial clauses for justification.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of Mediation:</b> Explaining concepts in simple words, rephrasing for understanding, and offering clear advice (e.g., "helps peers understand balanced diets by using simple words and two languages if needed").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration & Facilitation:</b> Guiding turn-taking and encouraging classmates to share ideas for the project.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer on a sticky note:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you explained simply today, and how did you do it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did you help your group members understand or share their ideas for the video project?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1a5276; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of mediating information (explaining or facilitating) felt easy for you today, and what felt challenging?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How will you apply the skills of simplifying information and giving clear advice in your final 'Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial'?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students mediate information and facilitate discussions? (e.g., specific activities, types of input).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for future mediation tasks or for the upcoming final project presentation? (e.g., more examples of bilingual mediation, sentence frames for facilitators).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the unit on "Why Is Nutrition Important?" The next steps will involve students finalizing their "Healthy Recipe Video Tutorial" projects for presentation, applying the mediation skills learned today in a comprehensive way for a real audience.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>